<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Inherits vanilla's LightMechanoidRecipe, the same base Vanilla Expanded's own 1.6 light
    mech recipes use, and overrides the three things that are actually ours: what it costs,
    where it is built and what research unlocks it.

    Writing it standalone was tempting - it is the only mech recipe here and inheritance can
    drag in a tier's ingredients by accident - but Inherit="False" on the ingredient list
    settles that, and the base carries several things worth having that are easy to get wrong
    by hand: formingTicks at vanilla's light-mech pace, the work amount, the working effecter
    and sound so the gestator actually looks and sounds busy, and workSpeedStat, without which
    Bill_Mech.WorkSpeedMultiplier returns a flat 1 and gestation ignores the mechanitor's
    stats - unlike every other mech in the game.

    Three fields carry the gestator contract, and all three are load-bearing:

      gestationCycles > 0   is what makes BillUtility.MakeNewBill hand back a Bill_ProductionMech
                            instead of a plain Bill_Production. Building_MechGestator.Tick casts
                            its active bill to Bill_Mech unconditionally, so a bill of any other
                            class on that table is a null reference on the next tick.

      products              must name a PAWN ThingDef. Bill_ProductionMech.CreateProducts looks
                            up the PawnKindDef whose race is this def and generates it, and
                            Notify_FormingCompleted casts the result to Pawn and reads its
                            kindDef. An item product would be a null reference there.

      mechanitorOnlyRecipe  keeps non-mechanitors out. Bill_Mech.PawnAllowedToStartAnew calls
                            p.mechanitor.HasBandwidthForBill, and p.mechanitor is null for
                            anyone without a mechlink; the base class's mechanitorOnlyRecipe
                            check runs first and returns false, which is what stops that being
                            a null reference. It is restated below even though the parent sets
                            it: it is redundant if inherited and it prevents a crash if it ever
                            is not, which is a trade worth one line.

    So gestating a Riimba needs a mechanitor, same as any mech. It costs that mechanitor no
    bandwidth once built, because the unit's BandwidthCost stat is 0 and its orders come from a
    control station instead - see Riimba.xml.
  -->

  <RecipeDef ParentName="LightMechanoidRecipe">
    <defName>Riimba_Gestate</defName>
    <label>gestate riimba</label>
    <description>Gestate a Riimba cleaning drone. Unlike a combat mech it carries no subcore of its own - the thinking is done by the control station that drives it, so a drone gestated with no station built is an expensive paperweight until one is.</description>
    <!-- One cycle. A Riimba is the cheapest thing the gestator can make. -->
    <gestationCycles>1</gestationCycles>
    <mechanitorOnlyRecipe>true</mechanitorOnlyRecipe>
    <researchPrerequisite>RiimbaCleaning</researchPrerequisite>
    <recipeUsers>
      <li>MechGestator</li>
    </recipeUsers>
    <!-- Inherit="False" so the light-mech tier's own ingredients, subcore included, are
         replaced rather than added to. A Riimba has no subcore: the station holds it. -->
    <ingredients Inherit="False">
      <li>
        <filter>
          <thingDefs>
            <li>Steel</li>
          </thingDefs>
        </filter>
        <count>60</count>
      </li>
      <li>
        <filter>
          <thingDefs>
            <li>ComponentIndustrial</li>
          </thingDefs>
        </filter>
        <count>3</count>
      </li>
    </ingredients>
    <fixedIngredientFilter Inherit="False">
      <thingDefs>
        <li>Steel</li>
        <li>ComponentIndustrial</li>
      </thingDefs>
    </fixedIngredientFilter>
    <products>
      <Riimba>1</Riimba>
    </products>
    <descriptionHyperlinks>
      <ThingDef>Riimba</ThingDef>
    </descriptionHyperlinks>
  </RecipeDef>

</Defs>
